Important difference: Target Memory vs Total Memory

These two metrics are extremely important for SQL Server DBAs.

Target Server Memory: Amount of memory SQL Server would like to commit based on current conditions and configuration.

Total Server Memory: Amount of memory SQL Server has currently committed.

Scenario

Interpretation

Total = Target

SQL Server has reached its current memory target

Total below Target

SQL Server may still be acquiring memory

Total below Target with low OS memory

Investigate OS pressure and configuration

Total below Target with sufficient OS memory

May simply be normal workload behavior

Important: Total Server Memory being lower than Target Server Memory does not automatically indicate a problem. Similarly, equal values do not guarantee that sufficient memory is available for every workload.

