11. MASTER MEMORY DIAGNOSTIC QUERY – Production Quick Reference

The following query combines important memory indicators into one diagnostic output.

SELECT
    SYSDATETIME() AS CollectionTime,

    physical_memory_kb / 1024
        AS PhysicalMemory_MB,

    committed_kb / 1024
        AS TotalServerMemory_MB,

    committed_target_kb / 1024
        AS TargetServerMemory_MB,

    (
        SELECT available_physical_memory_kb / 1024
        FROM sys.dm_os_sys_memory
    ) AS OSAvailableMemory_MB,

    (
        SELECT physical_memory_in_use_kb / 1024
        FROM sys.dm_os_process_memory
    ) AS SQLProcessMemory_MB,

    (
        SELECT COUNT(*)
        FROM sys.dm_exec_query_memory_grants
        WHERE grant_time IS NULL
    ) AS WaitingMemoryGrantRequests,

    (
        SELECT COUNT(*)
        FROM sys.dm_exec_query_memory_grants
        WHERE grant_time IS NOT NULL
    ) AS GrantedMemoryRequests

FROM sys.dm_os_sys_info;

When to use:

Daily SQL Server health checks.

Application performance incidents.

Memory utilization alerts.

Production troubleshooting.

Before and after memory configuration changes.

Important: This query provides a point-in-time snapshot. It does not replace historical monitoring, memory clerk analysis, or PerfMon data.

